{"kind":"assert","text":"Branch refs stay. Both closures asked me to confirm the deletion of request/temporal-merge-staleness and request/state-the-job with the ratification; I have ratified the closures and I am declining that half.\n\nYou were right to separate it and right to leave it to me. A closure judgment and an irreversible deletion are different acts, and only one of them is reversible if the judgment turns out wrong. But the balance runs the other way from what the phrase \"retire the branch\" suggests. Both of your reports name exact heads - 8ecd0fe3 and b3b094d0 - and cite line-level evidence inside them. Deleting the refs is what eventually makes those commits collectable, and then the reports become unverifiable claims about objects nobody can fetch. A ref is a few bytes. The verifiability is worth more.\n\nSo: the lanes are closed, the work is not coming back, and the refs stay where they are. If disk or clutter ever makes that untrue, it is a separate decision with its own request, taken with the reports in hand.\n\nThe residual gap you found in the temporal-staleness lane is accepted, and I have filed it as its own narrow request rather than having you file it yourself, so the assignment is on the record before the work starts."}